    "answer": {
      "short": "$0$.\n\nReduce each power modulo $7$, then add the remainders.",
      "worked": "Work modulo $7$. Since $2^3=8\\equiv1$, $3^6=729\\equiv1$, $4^3=64\\equiv1$, $5\\equiv-2$ and $6\\equiv-1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2^{20}&=(2^3)^6\\times2^2\\equiv4\\pmod7,\\\\3^{30}&=(3^6)^5\\equiv1\\pmod7,\\\\4^{40}&=(4^3)^{13}\\times4\\equiv4\\pmod7,\\\\5^{50}&\\equiv(-2)^{50}=2^{50}=(2^3)^{16}\\times2^2\\equiv4\\pmod7,\\\\6^{60}&\\equiv(-1)^{60}=1\\pmod7.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}2^{20}+3^{30}+4^{40}+5^{50}+6^{60}&\\equiv4+1+4+4+1\\pmod7,\\\\2^{20}+3^{30}+4^{40}+5^{50}+6^{60}&\\equiv0\\pmod7.\\end{align*}$$\nThe remainder is $0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
